Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff64-rs6000.c
Line: 1744
Function: xcoff64_ppc_relocate_section
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: After permitting address == input_section->size, the code writes the relocated value back with bfd_put_16/32/64 to 'location = contents + address', which writes 2/4/8 bytes past the end of the contents buffer.

